{#
settings/_signature.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The Signatures section: one editor per account, and per-address overrides
folded away behind a disclosure.

WHY IT LOOKS LIKE THIS
──────────────────────
The first version put a full editor on the account AND on every alias, all of
them open at once. An account with three aliases was four stacked editors —
about a screen and a half of settings for the overwhelmingly common wish,
which is "one signature, everywhere". So:

  • The account editor is the section. It is the only thing above the fold.
  • Everything per-address lives inside a <details>, which starts CLOSED when
    no address has an override — you do not pay in vertical space for a
    feature you have not asked for — and OPEN when one does, because
    configuration you already made must never be hidden from you.
  • An address that inherits is ONE LINE: the address, and a button. Not a
    card, not a greyed-out editor. There is no editor in the markup at all
    for it, which is also why the old "the field looks live until you toggle
    the checkbox" bug cannot come back: nothing is rendered, so nothing can
    be rendered in the wrong state.

THE THREE STATES, ON SCREEN
───────────────────────────
`getSetting(...) is null` is the whole distinction, and each state has its own
row shape rather than its own checkbox position:

  key absent      → "Uses the account signature" + [Use a different signature]
  key present ''  → an editor, empty, + [Use the account signature]
  key present HTML→ an editor with it,  + [Use the account signature]

Both buttons are plain form posts to SignatureController, so the state after
the click is whatever the server says it is. The previous design asked a
checkbox to mean the difference and then had to keep the editor's appearance
in step with it in JavaScript; this one has no client state to keep in step.

Variables:
  manageableAccounts  list<Account>
#}
{% if manageableAccounts is empty %}
    <p class="px-4 py-8 text-center text-sm text-ink-faint italic">
        {{ 'settings.accounts.empty'|trans }}
    </p>
{% else %}
    <div class="divide-y divide-line">
        {% for account in manageableAccounts %}
            {# Which aliases have an opinion of their own. Counted before the
               loop because it decides whether the disclosure starts open. #}
            {% set overridden = [] %}
            {% for alias in account.aliases %}
                {% if account.getSetting('compose.signature.alias.' ~ alias.id) is not null %}
                    {% set overridden = overridden|merge([alias.id]) %}
                {% endif %}
            {% endfor %}

            <div class="px-4 py-3.5">
                <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-ink-faint uppercase tracking-wider truncate mb-2">
                    {{ account.displayAddress }}
                </p>

                {# ── The account signature: the whole section, for most people ── #}
                <p class="text-sm text-ink">{{ 'settings.signature.label'|trans }}</p>
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-faint">{{ 'settings.signature.hint'|trans }}</p>

                {% include 'settings/_signature_editor.html.twig' with {
                    id:        'account-' ~ account.id,
                    action:    path('app_signature_default', { id: account.id }),
                    token:     csrf_token('settings-signature' ~ account.id),
                    signature: account.getSetting('compose.signature')|default(''),
                    label:     'settings.signature.label'|trans,
                } only %}

                {# ── Per-address overrides, folded away ───────────────────── #}
                {% if account.aliases|length %}
                    <details class="mt-3 group" {{ overridden|length ? 'open' : '' }}>
                        <summary class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer list-none
                                        text-xs text-ink-muted hover:text-ink transition-colors
                                        py-1 -mx-1 px-1 rounded">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-right w-3 text-ink-faint transition-transform
                                      group-open:rotate-90" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            <span>{{ 'settings.signature.per_address.disclosure'|trans }}</span>
                            {% if overridden|length %}
                                {# A bare number, with the sentence in an sr-only
                                   span: the badge sits next to the disclosure it
                                   counts, so sighted readers have the noun
                                   already and a screen reader would otherwise
                                   hear "3". #}
                                <span class="ml-auto shrink-0 rounded-full bg-raised px-2 py-0.5 text-[11px] text-ink-muted">
                                    {{ overridden|length }}
                                    <span class="sr-only">
                                        {{ 'settings.signature.per_address.count'|trans({'%number%': overridden|length}) }}
                                    </span>
                                </span>
                            {% endif %}
                        </summary>

                        <ul class="mt-1.5 divide-y divide-line/60">
                            {% for alias in account.aliases %}
                                {% set aliasSignature = account.getSetting('compose.signature.alias.' ~ alias.id) %}

                                <li class="settings-alias-row py-1.5"
                                    data-signature-alias="{{ alias.id }}"
                                    data-signature-state="{{ aliasSignature is null ? 'inherits' : 'overrides' }}">

                                    <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
                                        <span class="min-w-0 flex-1 truncate text-sm text-ink-muted">
                                            {{ alias.address }}
                                        </span>

                                        {# One button either way, and it always
                                           posts the state it names — so the row
                                           cannot disagree with what a click will
                                           do. #}
                                        <form method="post"
                                              action="{{ path('app_signature_alias', { id: account.id, aliasId: alias.id }) }}"
                                              data-turbo-stream
                                              class="shrink-0">
                                            <input type="hidden" name="_token"
                                                   value="{{ csrf_token('settings-signature-alias' ~ alias.id) }}">

                                            {% if aliasSignature is null %}
                                                <input type="hidden" name="override" value="1">
                                                <button type="submit"
                                                        class="rounded-full border border-line px-2.5 py-1 text-xs
                                                               text-ink-muted hover:bg-hover transition-colors">
                                                    {{ 'settings.signature.per_address.override'|trans }}
                                                    <span class="sr-only">
                                                        {{ 'settings.signature.per_address.override_for'|trans({'%alias%': alias.address}) }}
                                                    </span>
                                                </button>
                                            {% else %}
                                                <input type="hidden" name="inherit" value="1">
                                                <button type="submit"
                                                        class="rounded-full border border-line px-2.5 py-1 text-xs
                                                               text-ink-muted hover:bg-hover transition-colors">
                                                    {{ 'settings.signature.per_address.revert'|trans }}
                                                    <span class="sr-only">
                                                        {{ 'settings.signature.per_address.revert_for'|trans({'%alias%': alias.address}) }}
                                                    </span>
                                                </button>
                                            {% endif %}
                                        </form>
                                    </div>

                                    {% if aliasSignature is null %}
                                        {# The inheriting row ends here. One line,
                                           no editor, nothing disabled. #}
                                        <p class="text-xs text-ink-faint mt-0.5">
                                            {{ 'settings.signature.per_address.inherits'|trans }}
                                        </p>
                                    {% else %}
                                        {% include 'settings/_signature_editor.html.twig' with {
                                            id:        'alias-' ~ alias.id,
                                            action:    path('app_signature_alias', { id: account.id, aliasId: alias.id }),
                                            token:     csrf_token('settings-signature-alias' ~ alias.id),
                                            signature: aliasSignature,
                                            label:     'settings.signature.for_alias'|trans({'%alias%': alias.address}),
                                        } only %}

                                        {% if aliasSignature is empty %}
                                            <p class="text-xs text-ink-faint mt-1">
                                                {{ 'settings.signature.per_address.signs_with_nothing'|trans }}
                                            </p>
                                        {% endif %}
                                    {% endif %}
                                </li>
                            {% endfor %}
                        </ul>
                    </details>
                {% endif %}
            </div>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
{% endif %}
